  "description": "# Gwangju\n\n**KWJ · v0.4.0**\n\nCustom map of Gwangju, Korea, built from official Korean government transport and demographic data.\n\n## Coverage\n\n<table style=\"width: auto\">\n<tr><td><strong>Region</strong></td><td>광주광역시, 전라남도</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Playable Area</strong></td><td>1,609 km²</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<details>\n<summary>District list (10)</summary>\n\n<table style=\"width: auto\">\n<tr><th align=\"left\">시군구</th><th align=\"left\">District</th><th align=\"right\">Population</th></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"3\"><strong>광주광역시 (Gwangju)</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>광산구</td><td>Gwangsan-gu</td><td align=\"right\">453,001</td></tr>\n<tr><td>남구</td><td>Nam-gu</td><td align=\"right\">215,596</td></tr>\n<tr><td>동구</td><td>Dong-gu</td><td align=\"right\">151,241</td></tr>\n<tr><td>북구</td><td>Buk-gu</td><td align=\"right\">944,550</td></tr>\n<tr><td>서구</td><td>Seo-gu</td><td align=\"right\">463,003</td></tr>\n<tr><td colspan=\"3\"><strong>전라남도 (Jeollanam-do)</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td>나주시</td><td>Naju-si</td><td align=\"right\">127,384</td></tr>\n<tr><td>담양군</td><td>Damyang-gun</td><td align=\"right\">60,510</td></tr>\n<tr><td>여수시</td><td>Yeosu-si</td><td align=\"right\">39,389</td></tr>\n<tr><td>장성군</td><td>Jangseong-gun</td><td align=\"right\">33,557</td></tr>\n<tr><td>화순군</td><td>Hwasun-gun</td><td align=\"right\">148,114</td></tr>\n</table>\n</details>\n\n## Population Summary\n\n<table style=\"width: auto\">\n<tr><td><strong>Total Modeled Demand</strong></td><td align=\"right\">5,147,170</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Pops</strong></td><td align=\"right\">52,843</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n## Additional Features\n\n- **Neighborhood Labels** — The map includes municipal and neighborhood labels derived from administrative boundary data.\n\t- 시도 (Si, Do - Metropolitan / Provincial level)\n\t- 시군구 (Si, Gun, Gu - City / County / District level)\n\t- 읍면동 (Eup, Myeon, Dong - Neighborhood level)\n- **Special Demand POIs** — Airport, HSR station, Bus terminal, University, Hospital, School, Park, Shopping Center, Tourist Attraction, Ferry Terminal (where applicable); each modeled with real ridership, catchment gravity, or enrollment/visitor data.\n\n## Data Sources\n\n- Korean Transportation Database (Korea Transport Institute, KOTI) (ktdb.go.kr)\n- V-world (Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, MOLIT) (vworld.kr)\n- Statistical Geographic Information System (SGIS) plus (Ministry of Data and Statistics, MODS) (sgis.mods.go.kr)\n- Address-based Industry Support Service (Ministry of the Interior and Safety, MOIS) (business.juso.go.kr)\n- Aviation statistics 2025 (Korea Civil Aviation Association, KCAA) (airportal.go.kr)\n- Korean railroad statistics 2024 (Korea Railroad, KORAIL) (railstat.korail.com)\n- Korean Public Transportation Database (Korea Transportation Safety Authority, KTSA) (kotsa.or.kr)\n- Korean Hospital and Pharmacy Status (Health Insurance Review and Assessment Service, HIRA) (data.go.kr)\n- Health Insurance Medical Statistics (HIRA) (opendata.hira.or.kr)\n- Academy Information System (Ministry of Education, MOE) (academyinfo.go.kr)\n- School Info Disclosure (schoolinfo.go.kr) and Korea National Standard Data (data.go.kr) — schools, parks, shopping centers, tourist attractions\n- Korea Transport Safety Authority (KOMSA) coastal ferry statistics (komsa.or.kr)\n\n## Credits\n\nMap authored by budhakr",
